{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
My [G]Bonnie lies [C]over the [G]ocean,
My [G]Bonnie lies [A7]over the [D]sea,
My [G]Bonnie lies [C]over the [G]ocean,
Oh [C]bring back my [D]Bonnie to [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Bring back, [C]bring back,
Oh [D]bring back my Bonnie to [G]me, to me;
[G]Bring back, [C]bring back,
Oh [D]bring back my Bonnie to [G]me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
Oh [G]blow, ye winds, [C]over the [G]ocean,
And [G]blow, ye winds, [A7]over the [D]sea,
Oh [G]blow, ye winds, [C]over the [G]ocean,
And [C]bring back my [D]Bonnie to [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Last [G]night as I [C]lay on my [G]pillow,
Last [G]night as I [A7]lay on my [D]bed,
Last [G]night as I [C]lay on my [G]pillow,
I [C]dreamed that my [D]Bonnie was [G]dead.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}
The [G]winds have blown [C]over the [G]ocean,
The [G]winds have blown [A7]over the [D]sea,
The [G]winds have blown [C]over the [G]ocean,
And [C]brought back my [D]Bonnie to [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
